Build the software foundation for **STRIDE**, an AI-powered wearable navigation assistance system designed for blind and low-vision users.

## Project context

STRIDE is a 36–48-hour hackathon project for Hackachusetts 2026, built by three teammates. I am responsible exclusively for software development. The other two teammates handle the camera, electronics, ESP32 firmware, and physical assembly.

The system uses:

- MacBook Air M4 — FastAPI backend, database, AI processing
- iPhone 14 — accessible application interface
- AirPods Pro 3 — spoken guidance
- W11 ESP32-S3 with OV3660 — Wi-Fi image capture (camera hardware arriving later)
- ESP32 DevKit V1 with HC-SR04 — distance telemetry, local alerts, and motor feedback
- Gemini API — object and scene recognition
- SQLite — route, checkpoint, and sighting memory

The repository is named STRIDE. I am developing on `feature/software`.

